// Bundled ruleset — the floor of protection, shipped in the app so a failed
// or tampered fetch can never leave the user unprotected. Keep in sync with
// public/rules/spam-rules.json (that file may be NEWER; never older).
//
// `on`: name | collection | both | description | all
// `predicate`: a built-in check implemented in spam.js (things a regex can't
// express: contract anonymity, chain mismatch, entropy, image presence)
// `unless`: a built-in predicate that suppresses the rule
